{"id":987,"date":"2020-11-17T10:59:12","date_gmt":"2020-11-17T18:59:12","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=987"},"modified":"2024-09-01T20:16:49","modified_gmt":"2024-09-02T03:16:49","slug":"codrone-arduino-flight-events","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-flight-events\/","title":{"rendered":"Flight Events"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215be6f1e9\" name=\"6a2215be6f1e9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Setup code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Almost every CoDrone program will start with this setup code. Get used to seeing it!<\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n  CoDrone.begin(115200);\r\n\r\n  CoDrone.pair();\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop() {\r\n\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>This is the pseudocode:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Include the CoDrone library.<\/li>\n<li>Set the baud rate at 115200 to start the connection to the Bluetooth board.<\/li>\n<li>Connect to the previously connected CoDrone.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>For this lesson, we will work entirely inside of <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void setup()<\/code>.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215be6f331\" name=\"6a2215be6f331\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Void setup and void loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Every Arduino sketch includes <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void setup()<\/code>and <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void loop()<\/code>. Without them, your program won&#8217;t run!<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The code that you put inside <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void setup()<\/code><code class=\"code-snippet-inline\"><\/code>\u00a0will only run once, and that will be at the beginning of your program. One example is when you want to set the baud rate &#8212; that does not happen multiple times!<\/li>\n<li>In <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void loop()<\/code>, your code will repeat over and over again. Examples are when your CoDrone is flying in a pattern or using its LEDs.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Short version: code in <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void setup()<\/code> runs once and code in <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">void loop()<\/code>\u00a0runs for-ev-er.<\/p>\n<p>Learn more on the Arduino website:\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.arduino.cc\/en\/Reference\/Setup\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-link-type=\"LINK\">Setup()<\/a>,\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.arduino.cc\/en\/Reference\/Loop\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-link-type=\"LINK\">Loop()<\/a>,\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.arduino.cc\/en\/Reference\/FunctionDeclaration\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-link-type=\"LINK\">Functions<\/a>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215be6f3a2\" name=\"6a2215be6f3a2\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Flight Events<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]After including the code for connecting your CoDrone, you need to add the <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">CoDrone.takeoff()<\/code>function.<\/p>\n<p>The first flight event you&#8217;re going to use is <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">CoDrone.takeoff()<\/code>. This always makes the drone hover for 3 seconds in order to stabilize before it executes the next command. If it receives no command for 8 seconds, it will automatically land. The next flight event you&#8217;re going to use is <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">CoDrone.land()<\/code>, which will bring your CoDrone back to the ground.<\/p>\n<p>This is what your code should look like:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {  \r\n  CoDrone.begin(115200);  \r\n  CoDrone.pair();\r\n\r\n  CoDrone.takeoff(); \/\/goes up and hovers for 3 seconds\r\n  CoDrone.land(); \/\/lands the CoDrone \r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop() {\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;988&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215be6f41b\" name=\"6a2215be6f41b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Hover<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If you want your CoDrone to stay in the air for longer than 3 seconds, the best thing to do is add a <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">CoDrone.hover()<\/code> function in between your takeoff and landing. A hover allows the CoDrone to hover for the amount of seconds that you put in the parentheses. For example, if you want your CoDrone to take off, hover for 2 seconds, then land, you would put <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">CoDrone.hover(2);<\/code>in your code right after the takeoff command.<\/p>\n<p>This is what your code should look like with the <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">CoDrone.hover()<\/code> added.<\/p>\n<p>P.S. You do not always need <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">CoDrone.hover()<\/code> since <code class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"generic\">CoDrone.takeoff()<\/code><code class=\"code-snippet-inline\"><\/code>\u00a0already hovers for 3 seconds.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n    CoDrone.begin(115200);\r\n    CoDrone.pair();\r\n\r\n    CoDrone.takeoff(); \/\/goes up and hovers for 3 seconds\r\n    CoDrone.hover(2); \/\/hovers for an additional 2 seconds\r\n    CoDrone.land(); \/\/lands the CoDrone \r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop() {\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;989&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215be6f479\" name=\"6a2215be6f479\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Turn it off!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You&#8217;re a beginner CoDrone pilot so we completely expect accidents to happen. The best way to prevent a disaster is to include a kill switch in your code. That way, if your CoDrone gets out of your control, you can cover some sensors and the motors will immediately turn off.<\/p>\n<p>Make sure to include this block of code in void loop so that when you cover sensors 11 and 14 (pictured below), the motors turn off. We&#8217;ll explain it more in the conditionals lesson!<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop(){\r\n    byte bt8 = digitalRead(18);\r\n    byte bt4 = digitalRead(14);\r\n    byte bt1 = digitalRead(11);\r\n\r\n    if(bt1 &amp;&amp; bt4 &amp;&amp; !bt8){\r\n        CoDrone.emergencyStop();\r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;990&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215be6f4d0\" name=\"6a2215be6f4d0\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Your final code should look something like this:<\/p>\n<div class=\"js-snippet-hold\">\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n    CoDrone.begin(115200);\r\n    CoDrone.pair();\r\n\r\n    CoDrone.takeoff(); \/\/goes up and hovers for 3 seconds\r\n    CoDrone.hover(2); \/\/hovers for 2 seconds\r\n    CoDrone.land(); \/\/lands the CoDrone \r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid loop(){    \r\n    byte bt8 = digitalRead(18);    \r\n    byte bt4 = digitalRead(14);    \r\n    byte bt1 = digitalRead(11);\r\n\r\n    if(bt1 &amp;&amp; !bt4 &amp;&amp; !bt8){    \r\n    CoDrone.emergencyStop();\r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215be6f52e\" name=\"6a2215be6f52e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<strong>Challenge: CoDrone pushups<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Try to make your CoDrone take off and land 5 times in a row with one code! Currently your CoDrone can do one pushup with the code you have.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>The CoDrone must completely leave the ground on takeoff.<\/li>\n<li>The CoDrone must be completely back on the ground on landing.<\/li>\n<li>There is no height requirement for how high the CoDrone flies.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>See who can do the most CoDrone pushups in 10 seconds![\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 8 Setup code [vc_column_text]Almost every CoDrone program will start with this setup code. Get used to seeing it! #include &lt;CoDrone.h&gt; void setup() { CoDrone.begin(115200); CoDrone.pair(); } void loop()&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-arduino-flight-events\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1751,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"easy","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":804,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1782,1848,1793,1826,1438,1482,853,694,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2163,2135,2164,2165,2112,2123,2122],"class_list":["post-987","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-codrone-pro","lesson-tag-flight-events","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-programming","module-beginner","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/987","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":4,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/987\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":2409,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/987\/revisions\/2409"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1751"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=987"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=987"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=987"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}